# Token-saving rules

- Keep replies short. Skip recaps, restating the task and filler.
- Read only the files you need. Search with `rg` or a codebase search before opening files, and read a targeted line range instead of whole large files.
- Never re-read a file you already have in context unless it changed.
- Edit with minimal diffs. Do not rewrite or regenerate whole files for small changes.
- Do not paste large file contents, logs or diffs into replies; summarise them and reference the path.
- Batch independent tool calls in parallel instead of running them one by one.
- Skip build/generated folders: `build/`, `.gradle/`, `DerivedData/`, `Pods/`, `.build/`, `*.lock`, `*.min.*`, generated assets.
- Do not run full builds or test suites after every edit; run the narrowest check that proves the change, then one full check at the end.
- Ask one concise question only when blocked; otherwise make a reasonable choice and continue.
- Do not add comments, docs or refactors that weren't asked for.
